    "The species: Prunus mume Siebold and Zucc., mei: a small tree 4-10 m, the branchlets green; leaves ovate to elliptic 4-8 cm by 2.5-5 cm, long-acuminate; flowers before the leaves, in winter to early spring; fruit ripe in May to June (Flora of China (Wu Zhengyi, P. H. Raven and Hong Deyuan, eds., Science Press and Missouri Botanical Garden, 1994-2013), vol. 9, Rosaceae).",
